--
-- Notes:
-- 1. GRPPL Critical Care Franchisee (the 4-product sheet) contributes ZERO new rows —
--    every one of its SAP codes (5050807, 5043146, 5040019, 5040287) is a verbatim
--    duplicate of a row already present in the GRPPL Franchisee sheet. Confirmed by
--    cross-checking SAP codes across both documents before writing this file.
-- 2. KNOWN SOURCE-DATA CONFLICT: the Axera Trion sheet lists two different products
--    ("TELMICLAR AM TAB 40/5MG,15'S" and "TELMICLAR TAB 40MG,15'S") both under SAP
--    code 5602597. Since sap_code has a unique constraint, TELMICLAR TAB's sap_code is
--    left NULL here rather than guessing a correct value — flag this to Florus for the
--    real, distinct SAP code before it matters for ordering/invoicing.
-- 3. Uses ON CONFLICT (sap_code) DO NOTHING — the 23 products from the Checkpoint 2
--    sample seed are already present and will simply be skipped, not duplicated or
--    overwritten. NULL sap_codes never conflict with each other under a unique
--    constraint, so upcoming/unresolved-SAP-code rows insert safely regardless of order.
-- 4. Categories referenced here must already exist (seeded in Checkpoint 2 — all 17).

